---
import NerdBox from "@/components/caira/NerdBox.astro";
---

<div class="reveal">
  <div class="fig">
    <svg
      viewBox="0 0 720 200"
      role="img"
      aria-label="Grounding pipeline: facts in, model writes, shape check, sanitizer, send, five stations left to right, with a red branch from shape check and sanitizer dropping to a bin labelled let me check with the clinic"
    >
      <defs>
        <marker
          id="gp-ar"
          markerWidth="8"
          markerHeight="8"
          refX="6.5"
          refY="3.5"
          orient="auto"
        >
          <path d="M0,0 L7,3.5 L0,7 z" style="fill:var(--cx-teal)"></path>
        </marker>
        <marker
          id="gp-arR"
          markerWidth="8"
          markerHeight="8"
          refX="6.5"
          refY="3.5"
          orient="auto"
        >
          <path d="M0,0 L7,3.5 L0,7 z" style="fill:var(--cx-red)"></path>
        </marker>
        <style is:inline>
          .gpbox {
            fill: var(--cx-ink3);
            stroke: var(--cx-line2);
            stroke-width: 1;
          }
          .gplbl {
            font-family: var(--cx-mono);
            font-size: 10px;
            font-weight: 700;
            fill: var(--cx-text);
            text-anchor: middle;
          }
          .gpsub {
            font-family: var(--cx-mono);
            font-size: 7.5px;
            fill: var(--cx-muted);
            text-anchor: middle;
          }
          .gpline {
            stroke: var(--cx-teal);
            stroke-width: 1.6;
            fill: none;
            marker-end: url(#gp-ar);
          }
          .gpred {
            stroke: var(--cx-red);
            stroke-width: 1.5;
            fill: none;
            marker-end: url(#gp-arR);
          }
          .gpbin {
            fill: var(--cx-ink4);
            stroke: var(--cx-red);
            stroke-width: 1.4;
          }
          .gpbinlbl {
            font-family: var(--cx-mono);
            font-size: 8.5px;
            fill: var(--cx-red-soft);
            text-anchor: middle;
          }
        </style>
      </defs>

      <rect class="gpbox" x="14" y="40" width="120" height="50" rx="9"></rect>
      <text class="gplbl" x="74" y="61">facts in</text>
      <text class="gpsub" x="74" y="76">fenced markers</text>

      <rect class="gpbox" x="158" y="40" width="120" height="50" rx="9"></rect>
      <text class="gplbl" x="218" y="61">model writes</text>
      <text class="gpsub" x="218" y="76">JSON only</text>

      <rect class="gpbox" x="302" y="40" width="120" height="50" rx="9"></rect>
      <text class="gplbl" x="362" y="61">shape check</text>
      <text class="gpsub" x="362" y="76">Zod schema</text>

      <rect class="gpbox" x="446" y="40" width="120" height="50" rx="9"></rect>
      <text class="gplbl" x="506" y="58">sanitizer</text>
      <text class="gpsub" x="506" y="71">links stripped</text>
      <text class="gpsub" x="506" y="82">length capped</text>

      <rect class="gpbox" x="590" y="40" width="116" height="50" rx="9"></rect>
      <text class="gplbl" x="648" y="61">send</text>
      <text class="gpsub" x="648" y="76">to the patient</text>

      <line class="gpline flow-dash" x1="134" y1="65" x2="156" y2="65"></line>
      <line class="gpline flow-dash" x1="278" y1="65" x2="300" y2="65"></line>
      <line class="gpline flow-dash" x1="422" y1="65" x2="444" y2="65"></line>
      <line class="gpline flow-dash" x1="566" y1="65" x2="588" y2="65"></line>

      <rect class="gpbin" x="290" y="152" width="220" height="38" rx="9"></rect>
      <text class="gpbinlbl" x="400" y="175"
        >"let me check with the clinic"</text
      >

      <path class="gpred flow-dash" d="M362,90 L362,120 L400,120 L400,150"
      ></path>
      <path class="gpred flow-dash" d="M506,90 L506,130 L400,130 L400,150"
      ></path>
    </svg>
    <div class="figcap">
      Teal: the happy path, five stations, one direction. Red: anything shape
      check or the sanitizer rejects falls straight to the same safe sentence,
      never back into the model for a retry.
    </div>
  </div>

  <NerdBox title="the three walls, in code">
    <p>
      The prompt fences the clinic's facts between explicit markers and asks for
      JSON only, a request the model can ignore. The response is checked against
      a Zod schema, and the sanitizer strips every link and caps the reply
      length, an actual guarantee. The provider stack itself is a decorator
      chain, cache then fallback then metering then vendor, so a slow or dead
      model degrades instead of taking the feature down. Feed her a prompt
      injection and the classifier tags it, grounding still checks it against
      the clinic's real facts, finds nothing there, and the whole thing falls
      back to the same polite handoff a real failure would produce.
    </p>
  </NerdBox>
</div>
